[112.9084, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 21 \u001b[22m     \u001b[38;5;148manchors:\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m 22 -\u001b[38;5;231m      no: \"The message only names a problem, bug, symptom or goal (e.g. 'fix X bug'\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m    -\u001b[38;5;231m, 'X is nullable', 'make Y less flaky') without saying what change was made to the \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m    -\u001b[38;5;231mcode, so a reader cannot tell what was actually done\"                              \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m 23 -\u001b[38;5;231m      yes: \"The message summarises the code change: the object of change, a list of\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m    -\u001b[38;5;231m changes, before/after, what the changed code now does, or how the change works\"   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 22 +\u001b[38;5;231m      \u001b[38;5;148mno:\u001b[38;5;231m \u001b[38;5;186m\"The message describes only the problem, symptom or desired outcome and n\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m    +\u001b[38;5;186mever says which change was made\"\u001b[38;5;231m                                                   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 23 +\u001b[38;5;231m      \u001b[38;5;148myes:\u001b[38;5;231m \u001b[38;5;186m\"The message says what was changed, even briefly: naming the object of c\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m    +\u001b[38;5;186mhange and the kind of change (add, remove, update, rename, polish, fix in a named f\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m    +\u001b[38;5;186mile or component) is enough. A change list, a before/after contrast, what the code \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m    +\u001b[38;5;186mnow does, or how the change works also count\"\u001b[38;5;231m                                      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 24 \u001b[22m \u001b[38;5;148maggregation:\u001b[38;5;231m { \u001b[38;5;148mmethod:\u001b[38;5;231m \u001b[38;5;186mmin\u001b[38;5;231m, \u001b[38;5;148mpassThreshold:\u001b[38;5;231m \u001b[38;5;141m50\u001b[38;5;231m }\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246mCalled verdict \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39mCheck 7 reached 78% agreement, with most remaining misses being humans-good messages the combined\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153mgood\u001b[39m criterion rejects for lacking a reason. I'm replacing \u001b[38;5;153mgood\u001b[39m with a pure \u001b[38;5;153mwhy\u001b[39m criterion that\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Buses the codebook's list of reason types next.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39mReading\u001b[11G\u001b[1m1\u001b[13G\u001b[22mfile\u2026\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf  commit-review.yaml\u001b[25G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[29C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;246m8\u001b[39G)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
